index 00000000..d8a86fc7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/cluster/cz.vpsfree/containers/prg/proxy/prometheus-query.nix
@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@
+{ lib }:
+let
+  authFile = "/var/lib/nginx-auth/prometheus-codex.htpasswd";
+  postEndpoints = [
+    "query"
+    "query_range"
+    "series"
+    "labels"
+  ];
+  getEndpoints = [
+    "metadata"
+    "targets"
+    "targets/metadata"
+    "rules"
+    "alerts"
+    "status/buildinfo"
+    "status/runtimeinfo"
+  ];
+  labelValues = "label/[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*/values";
+
+  location = upstream: endpoint: methods: {
+    basicAuthFile = authFile;
+    proxyPass = upstream;
+    recommendedProxySettings = false;
+    extraConfig = ''
+      # Reject alternate raw spellings before rewriting the normalized URI.
+      if ($request_uri !~ "^/codex/api/v1/${endpoint}([?]|$)") { return 404; }
+      if ($request_method !~ "^(${methods})$") { return 405; }
+      rewrite ^/codex(/api/v1/.*)$ $1 break;
+      proxy_set_header Authorization "";
+      proxy_set_header Host $host;
+      proxy_set_header Connection "";
+      proxy_http_version 1.1;
+      proxy_connect_timeout 5s;
+      proxy_send_timeout 15s;
+      proxy_read_timeout 30s;
+      client_max_body_size 64k;
+      client_body_timeout 10s;
+      limit_req zone=prometheus_codex_rate burst=5 nodelay;
+      limit_req_status 429;
+      limit_conn prometheus_codex_connections 4;
+      limit_conn_status 429;
+    '';
+  };
+in
+{
+  # A constant key shares both budgets across vhosts and unauthenticated clients.
+  # $remote_user is unavailable when nginx runs its limit phases.
+  httpConfig = ''
+    limit_req_zone prometheus-codex zone=prometheus_codex_rate:1m rate=2r/s;
+    limit_conn_zone prometheus-codex zone=prometheus_codex_connections:1m;
+  '';
+
+  locations =
+    upstream:
+    lib.listToAttrs (
+      map (
+        endpoint:
+        lib.nameValuePair "= /codex/api/v1/${endpoint}" (location upstream endpoint "GET|HEAD|POST")
+      ) postEndpoints
+      ++ map (
+        endpoint: lib.nameValuePair "= /codex/api/v1/${endpoint}" (location upstream endpoint "GET|HEAD")
+      ) getEndpoints
+    )
+    // {
+      "~ ^/codex/api/v1/${labelValues}$" = location upstream labelValues "GET|HEAD";
+      "= /codex".return = 404;
+      "/codex/".return = 404;
+    };
+}
diff --git a/docs/operations/log-reader-access.md b/docs/operations/log-reader-access.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..af3c4b21
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/operations/log-reader-access.md
@@ -0,0 +1,150 @@
+# Log reader access
+
+The Prague logger provides the `log-reader` SSH account for inspecting collected
+logs with ordinary commands such as `grep` and `tail`. Its root-managed public
+key is the existing aitherdev machine key. There is no source-address restriction.
+
+```sh
+ssh -T log-reader@log.int.prg.vpsfree.cz \
+  'tail -n 100 /var/log/remote/cz.vpsfree/nodes/prg/node1/log'
+ssh -T log-reader@log.int.prg.vpsfree.cz \
+  'grep -F "search text" /var/log/messages'
+```
+
+Use the normal SSH identity selection on aitherdev if the machine key is not
+selected automatically. Bound searches by host, date or output size where
+possible. All selected log contents are readable without redaction.
+
+## Access boundary
+
+The account belongs only to `log-readers`. Remote log directories are owned by
+`root:log-readers` with mode `0750`; regular logs and messages archives use
+`0640`. Rsyslog applies that policy when creating new files and host directories.
+Logrotate creates replacements as `0640 root log-readers`, retaining the existing
+daily/monthly schedules, retention, date suffixes, uncompressed files and rsyslog
+HUP. The exporter pipe retains its own group and mode.
+
+The reader cannot directly overwrite, truncate, delete or rename those logs or
+change production configuration. It has no sudo, wheel membership, Nix trust or
+service-control grant. SSH permits public-key authentication only and disables
+PTYs, TCP/Unix-socket/agent/X11 forwarding, tunnels and user rc execution. Only
+`/etc/ssh/authorized_keys.d/log-reader` supplies authorized keys; keys in the
+writable home cannot override these restrictions.
+
+This is an ordinary unprivileged shell. It can write its home and `/tmp`, run
+programs, create sockets, connect outbound and generate ordinary log messages.
+It has no resource sandbox or per-session isolation. Other processes using the
+same Unix account share its access.
+
+## Historical permissions
+
+Configuration activation does not rewrite historical metadata. Before enabling
+routine reader use, an authorized operator must inspect the existing readers and
+reconcile the selected files. This is a separate operation from deploying the
+configuration; the commands below have no automatic activation hook.
+
+`log-reader-reconcile` handles only `/var/log/remote` and its descendants, plus
+`/var/log/messages` and its date-suffixed or numbered archives (optional `.gz`).
+It inventories directories and regular files without reading log contents. It
+does not change `/var/log` itself, the exporter pipe or unrelated log trees.
+The default bounds are 100,000 entries and 32 directory levels. Exceeding either
+refuses the operation; choose a larger explicit bound only after inspecting why
+the tree exceeds the expected size.
+
+The helper refuses symlinks, special files, hard-linked files, mount points
+inside the scope (including bind mounts), foreign filesystems, non-root owners,
+groups other than `root`/`log-readers`, extended/default POSIX ACLs, special mode
+bits and group/other write permissions. It opens paths relative to directory
+descriptors with no symlink following. `/var/log` and its parents must already be
+root-owned and protected from group/other writes; `/var/log` must permit reader
+traversal. These refusals require inspection rather than a recursive chmod.
+
+Before taking the inventory:
+
+1. Identify every service or operator that needs the old group/ACL/world-read
+   access. Preserve required non-root readers with declarative membership in
+   `log-readers`, under the usual configuration review process. Broader existing
+   access is intentionally removed by the new modes.
+2. Inspect any refusal with `stat` and `getfacl -p -- EXACT_PATH`. Save its original
+   owner, group, mode and ACL in a private recovery record. Resolve only the
+   inspected paths: for example, after preserving an existing reader's access,
+   replace its old group with `log-readers` using `chgrp`, or remove a redundant
+   ACL with `setfacl -b` (and `setfacl -k` for a default directory ACL). Do not
+   remove an ACL or change a group until its readers are accounted for. Unknown
+   owners, links, special files or mounts need their own diagnosis.
+3. Schedule a brief logging maintenance window. Stop rotation and quiesce input
+   with `systemctl stop logrotate.timer logrotate.service` followed by
+   `systemctl stop syslog.service syslog.socket`. Remote senders may queue or
+   lose messages according to their transport; do not leave ingestion stopped.
+   Ensure no other root process rotates or changes the selected tree.
+
+Then, as root on the logger:
+
+```sh
+install -d -m 0700 /root/log-reader-recovery
+log-reader-reconcile \
+  --inventory /root/log-reader-recovery/before.json
+```
+
+The inventory is created exclusively with mode `0600`; an existing output file
+causes refusal. It records the path, device/inode, owner/group, mode and file kind
+for each selected entry. Review it before applying. Keep it on the logger or in
+private operator storage, outside this repository.
+
+```sh
+log-reader-reconcile --apply /root/log-reader-recovery/before.json
+systemctl start syslog.socket syslog.service
+systemctl start logrotate.timer
+```
+
+Apply rescans the full bounded scope and requires the reviewed metadata and
+identities to match before writing. It changes only group/mode, retaining root
+ownership and log contents. Reapplying the same inventory after a successful
+application is supported when the scope and identities are unchanged. New files,
+rotation or other metadata changes require a fresh inventory and review. A
+failure before apply writes nothing; a failure during apply can leave some
+entries reconciled. Inspect them against the retained inventory before retrying,
+and restore ingestion promptly even when reconciliation fails.
+
+## Acceptance, revocation and recovery
+
+After deployment and reconciliation, verify bounded reads from current remote
+logs, historical remote logs, `/var/log/messages` and its archives through the
+reader account. Observe normal ingestion and exporter health, a newly appearing
+host directory, and an ordinary scheduled rotation. Confirm the resulting
+files/directories use the expected owner/group/modes. Test destructive denials
+only in a disposable fixture; do not probe production by truncating or deleting
+logs.
+
+The aitherdev key may also be manually authorized for root on the logger.
+Deploying this account does not revoke that grant. After reader acceptance,
+the user removes that manual root authorized-key entry personally. The
+configuration and reconciliation helper never edit root's authorized keys.
+
+Revoke reader access by removing its configured public key and deploying the
+change; end already-open sessions separately if immediate revocation is needed.
+Reverting configuration does not undo historical group/mode changes. For a
+metadata rollback, first disable reader access, quiesce rotation/ingestion, then
+restore only reviewed paths whose device/inode still match the saved inventory,
+using their recorded owner/group/mode and any separately saved ACLs. Do not apply
+old metadata to replacements created by rotation. The helper does not automate
+rollback. Retain logs and the exporter pipe; never restore root key access as a
+side effect of recovery.
+
+## Disposable verification
+
+The `log-reader-access` flake check evaluates the account, key, log creation and
+rotation policy and checks rsyslog/Python syntax. Its `vmTest` attribute runs
+the production logger rules with a synthetic public key and exporter consumer:
+
+```sh
+nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.log-reader-access
+nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.log-reader-access.vmTest
+```
+
+The VM covers historical reconciliation/refusals, new-host ingestion, exporter
+output, SSH restrictions and home-key rejection, protected-file denials, and
+current/archive access across rotation. Run the VM and affected-host builds
+through the development session's verification watcher after final review.
+Disposable tests do not establish production ownership, ACLs or reader lists;
+those remain rollout checks.
diff --git a/docs/operations/prometheus-query-access.md b/docs/operations/prometheus-query-access.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..ae73eedb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/operations/prometheus-query-access.md
@@ -0,0 +1,277 @@
+# Prometheus query access
+
+The Prague HTTPS proxy exposes a dedicated authenticated API at:
+
+- `https://mon1.prg.vpsfree.cz/codex/api/v1`
+- `https://mon2.prg.vpsfree.cz/codex/api/v1`
+
+Each address queries its own Prometheus instance. Mon1 retains up to 365 days
+or 500 GB; mon2 retains up to 30 days or 60 GB. Actual history depends on ingestion
+and the first retention limit reached. Public HTTPS routing needs no private
+address mapping or change to aitherdev. Raw port 9090 remains restricted.
+
+The dedicated Basic username is `codex-aitherdev`. Its password is a separately
+generated 32-byte random value encoded as 64 hexadecimal characters. Human
+credentials remain in `/private/nginx/mon.htpasswd`: they do not authenticate
+dedicated routes, and the dedicated credential does not unlock the human UI or
+other API routes. This separation applies on both monitors.
+
+## API boundary and limits
+
+Paths below are relative to `/codex/api/v1`. Only these exact routes are allowed:
+
+| Paths | Methods |
+| --- | --- |
+| `/query`, `/query_range`, `/series`, `/labels` | GET, POST |
+| `/label/<name>/values` | GET |
+| `/metadata`, `/targets`, `/targets/metadata`, `/rules`, `/alerts` | GET |
+| `/status/buildinfo`, `/status/runtimeinfo` | GET |
+
+HEAD accompanies GET. Label names use `[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*` in a single path
+segment. Trailing slashes, encoded path spellings and unlisted paths or methods
+are rejected. Query strings and form POST bodies pass through unchanged. Nginx
+removes `/codex` and the `Authorization` header before contacting Prometheus.
+Admin/TSDB mutation, reload/quit, receivers, remote read, config/flags, debugging,
+federation and UI routes are unavailable through this credential.
+
+The new routes share one budget across both vhosts: 2 requests/s with a burst
+of 5 and at most 4 active requests. Excess requests receive HTTP 429. The fixed
+quota key also counts unauthenticated requests; public clients can exhaust the
+quota. Human UI and Grafana requests do not use it. Bodies are limited to 64 KiB,
+with a 10s body timeout. Upstream connect/send/read timeouts are 5s/15s/30s.
+The read timeout measures inactivity, not total execution time or CPU use.
+
+Use bounded ranges and `timeout=20s` in queries. That timeout is client courtesy,
+not an enforced proxy CPU budget. The credential can read all metrics and the
+listed operational metadata, without tenant isolation or redaction.
+
+## Runtime credential files
+
+Provision these outside Git and Nix before activating the query policy:
+
+| Host and file | Owner | Mode | Contents |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Proxy: `/var/lib/nginx-auth` | `root:nginx` | `0750` | Dedicated directory |
+| Proxy: `/var/lib/nginx-auth/prometheus-codex.htpasswd` | `root:nginx` | `0640` | One username and bcrypt cost-8 hash |
+| Aitherdev: `/home/aither/.config/vpsfree-observability` | `aither:users` | `0700` | Dedicated directory |
+| Aitherdev: `/home/aither/.config/vpsfree-observability/prometheus.curlrc` | `aither:users` | `0600` | Basic credential and HTTPS curl defaults |
+
+Only the server pathname appears in Nix. Do not use `basicAuth`, `readFile`,
+`writeText`, Home Manager content/source, or a Nix-generated credential file.
+Neither plaintext nor the hash belongs in Git, the Nix store, command arguments,
+environment variables, shell history, logs or chat. A missing runtime hash file
+fails closed. Build and activation do not generate a default credential.
+
+Inspect the paths, mounts and ACLs before provisioning. Stop on unexpected
+symlinks, foreign ownership, ACL grants or mounts rather than repairing them
+blindly. Leave `/private` permissions and the human password file alone. File
+permissions protect against other users; processes and sessions running as
+`aither`, and root, can read the client credential.
+
+### Provision or rotate
+
+This is an operator procedure, separate from source builds and deployment.
+Run it as `aither` on aitherdev, from a private terminal with shell tracing,
+session recording and command-output capture disabled. Verify the proxy SSH host
+key first. The proxy needs `python3` and `htpasswd` in the root SSH command's
+PATH; `htpasswd` is supplied by its configured Apache package. Prepare any
+temporary Python environment separately if needed.
+
+The following example replaces the whole dedicated password file. It generates
+the password in memory, passes it over SSH stdin to `htpasswd -i -B -C 8`, and
+stages both files in their destination directories before atomic replacement.
+It never prints the password or hash. Existing paths must already have the
+documented ownership and modes. A failure after the server replacement can leave
+the previous client credential invalid; rerun the procedure to recover with a
+fresh credential. It does not change the human password file.
+
+```sh
+umask 077
+python3 - <<'PY'
+import grp
+import os
+from pathlib import Path
+import pwd
+import secrets
+import shlex
+import stat
+import subprocess
+import tempfile
+
+remote = r'''
+import grp
+import os
+from pathlib import Path
+import re
+import stat
+import subprocess
+import sys
+import tempfile
+
+def check(path, uid, gid, mode, directory):
+    s = path.lstat()
+    kind = stat.S_ISDIR if directory else stat.S_ISREG
+    if not kind(s.st_mode) or (s.st_uid, s.st_gid, stat.S_IMODE(s.st_mode)) != (uid, gid, mode):
+        raise RuntimeError("Unexpected credential path metadata: " + str(path))
+
+if os.geteuid() != 0:
+    raise RuntimeError("Proxy provisioning requires root")
+for ancestor in [Path("/var"), Path("/var/lib")]:
+    s = ancestor.lstat()
+    if not stat.S_ISDIR(s.st_mode) or s.st_uid != 0 or s.st_mode & 0o022:
+        raise RuntimeError("Unexpected server ancestor metadata")
+gid = grp.getgrnam("nginx").gr_gid
+parent = Path("/var/lib/nginx-auth")
+if not parent.exists() and not parent.is_symlink():
+    parent.mkdir(mode=0o750)
+    os.chown(parent, 0, gid)
+check(parent, 0, gid, 0o750, True)
+target = parent / "prometheus-codex.htpasswd"
+if target.exists() or target.is_symlink():
+    check(target, 0, gid, 0o640, False)
+password = sys.stdin.readline().rstrip("\n")
+if re.fullmatch(r"[0-9a-f]{64}", password) is None:
+    raise RuntimeError("Invalid generated password format")
+hashed = subprocess.run(
+    ["htpasswd", "-niBC", "8", "codex-aitherdev"],
+    input=password + "\n", text=True, capture_output=True, check=True,
+).stdout.strip() + "\n"
+if re.fullmatch(r"codex-aitherdev:\$2[aby]\$08\$[./A-Za-z0-9]{53}\n", hashed) is None:
+    raise RuntimeError("Unexpected htpasswd output format")
+fd, temporary = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=".prometheus-", dir=parent)
+try:
+    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as output:
+        os.fchown(output.fileno(), 0, gid)
+        os.fchmod(output.fileno(), 0o640)
+        output.write(hashed)
+        output.flush()
+        os.fsync(output.fileno())
+    os.replace(temporary, target)
+finally:
+    if os.path.exists(temporary):
+        os.unlink(temporary)
+'''
+
+uid = pwd.getpwnam("aither").pw_uid
+gid = grp.getgrnam("users").gr_gid
+if os.geteuid() != uid:
+    raise RuntimeError("Run this procedure as aither")
+for ancestor in [Path("/home"), Path("/home/aither"), Path("/home/aither/.config")]:
+    s = ancestor.lstat()
+    owner = 0 if ancestor == Path("/home") else uid
+    if not stat.S_ISDIR(s.st_mode) or s.st_uid != owner or s.st_mode & 0o022:
+        raise RuntimeError("Unexpected client ancestor metadata")
+parent = Path("/home/aither/.config/vpsfree-observability")
+if not parent.exists() and not parent.is_symlink():
+    parent.mkdir(mode=0o700)
+    os.chown(parent, uid, gid)
+target = parent / "prometheus.curlrc"
+for path, mode, directory in [(parent, 0o700, True), (target, 0o600, False)]:
+    if path.exists() or path.is_symlink():
+        s = path.lstat()
+        kind = stat.S_ISDIR if directory else stat.S_ISREG
+        if not kind(s.st_mode) or (s.st_uid, s.st_gid, stat.S_IMODE(s.st_mode)) != (uid, gid, mode):
+            raise RuntimeError("Unexpected client credential metadata")
+password = secrets.token_hex(32)
+client = (
+    'user = "codex-aitherdev:' + password + '"\n'
+    'basic\nfail\nsilent\nshow-error\nproto = "=https"\n'
+    'proto-redir = "=https"\nconnect-timeout = 5\nmax-time = 45\n'
+)
+fd, temporary = tempfile.mkstemp(prefix=".prometheus-", dir=parent)
+try:
+    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as output:
+        os.fchown(output.fileno(), uid, gid)
+        os.fchmod(output.fileno(), 0o600)
+        output.write(client)
+        output.flush()
+        os.fsync(output.fileno())
+    subprocess.run(
+        ["ssh", "-T", "root@proxy.prg.vpsfree.cz", "python3 -c " + shlex.quote(remote)],
+        input=password + "\n", text=True, check=True,
+    )
+    os.replace(temporary, target)
+finally:
+    if os.path.exists(temporary):
+        os.unlink(temporary)
+PY
+```
+
+The password has no automatic expiry. Rotate after suspected disclosure or
+when access ownership changes. For ordinary rotation, atomically replace the
+hash entry and client config as above. A brief HTTP 401 gap is acceptable.
+Nginx reads the runtime password file for each request, so routine file rotation
+does not need a reload or restart. If overlap is required, use distinct usernames
+and explicitly retire the old one; duplicate entries for one username do not
+provide reliable overlap.
+
+To revoke access, atomically replace the dedicated file with an empty regular
+file at `root:nginx 0640` in the same directory, or remove the old username entry
+while preserving separately approved users. Remove the unused client file.
+New requests then fail authentication, including on existing keepalive/HTTP/2
+connections; requests already executing are not canceled. Do not use credential
+rotation as a substitute for investigating a compromised account.
+
+## Query from aitherdev
+
+Use `-q` as curl's first option to suppress a global/default curlrc, followed
+by the explicit private config and a fixed HTTPS URL:
+
+```sh
+curl -q --config /home/aither/.config/vpsfree-observability/prometheus.curlrc \
+  --get --data-urlencode 'query=up' --data-urlencode 'timeout=20s' \
+  https://mon1.prg.vpsfree.cz/codex/api/v1/query
+
+curl -q --config /home/aither/.config/vpsfree-observability/prometheus.curlrc \
+  --data-urlencode 'query=sum(up)' --data-urlencode 'timeout=20s' \
+  https://mon2.prg.vpsfree.cz/codex/api/v1/query
+
+curl -q --config /home/aither/.config/vpsfree-observability/prometheus.curlrc \
+  --get --data-urlencode 'query=up' \
+  --data-urlencode 'start=2026-10-20T12:00:00Z' \
+  --data-urlencode 'end=2026-10-20T12:10:00Z' \
+  --data-urlencode 'step=60s' --data-urlencode 'timeout=20s' \
+  https://mon1.prg.vpsfree.cz/codex/api/v1/query_range
+```
+
+Choose a recent interval within the selected monitor's retention for range
+queries. Keep credentials out of URLs and command arguments. Do not add `-u`,
+`-k`/`--insecure`, redirect following, verbose/trace output, or a global curlrc.
+The config enforces HTTPS, normal certificate validation, a 5s connection timeout
+and a 45s total client timeout. There is no client wrapper or system deployment.
+
+## Verification and recovery
+
+The flake check `prometheus-query-access` evaluates the production vhost policy
+and checks nginx syntax using disposable runtime paths. Its `integration`
+passthru runs both vhosts against permissive local stubs with synthetic
+credentials. It covers GET/form POST routing, query/body preservation,
+Authorization removal, method/path/normalization denial, separate human auth,
+missing/wrong credentials, body/rate/concurrency limits, and rotation/revocation
+on existing HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 connections. Run the longer integration fixture
+after independent review, through the workspace verification watcher:
+
+```sh
+nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.prometheus-query-access
+nix build .#checks.x86_64-linux.prometheus-query-access.integration
+```
+
+Live acceptance needs separate deployment authorization. Prepare the server
+file before activating the proxy configuration. Use bounded reads to verify
+both public HTTPS addresses, the expected separate backends, human UI access,
+and failure with missing/wrong dedicated credentials. Confirm old/new credential
+behavior after rotation without printing either credential or HTTP headers.
+Do not run destructive API probes against production. The local fixture does
+not certify public TLS, deployed runtime ownership, or live availability.
+
+Configuration rollback removes dedicated API access. Credential file changes
+are independent of Nix generations; rolling back Nix does not restore an old
+password. Retain the intended runtime files or revoke them explicitly. Do not
+roll back by adding this credential to the human password file or opening raw
+Prometheus access. Logger access and its separate manual root-key removal are
+described in [log reader access](log-reader-access.md).
+
+See the upstream [nginx Basic auth](https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_auth_basic_module.html),
+[proxy](https://nginx.org/en/docs/http/ngx_http_proxy_module.html),
+[htpasswd](https://httpd.apache.org/docs/2.4/programs/htpasswd.html) and
+[curl](https://curl.se/docs/manpage.html) references for the underlying interfaces.
